# The gen-l10n report of keys present in the template and missing from a
# translation (see l10n.yaml). A build artifact, regenerated on every run — CI
# fails when it is non-empty.
l10n_untranslated.json

# The generated string table.
#
# Not committed, and the .g.dart precedent does not transfer. build_runner is
# slow, needs its own dependency tree and describes a database schema, so
# committing its output buys real time and a real diff. `flutter gen-l10n` runs
# automatically as part of `flutter pub get` (pubspec: generate: true), takes
# about two seconds, and reads nothing but the two .arb files beside it — so
# there is no window in which a checkout has the .arb and not the table.
#
# This was committed once, and the argument for it was circular: a committed
# table can go stale, so CI diffed it against a fresh generate to prove it
# hadn't — a gate guarding a defect that only existed because of the decision to
# commit. It cost 4.8 lines of generated churn per line of .arb (+8,253 against
# +1,715 over its lifetime), and a two-line translation fix arrived as a
# fourteen-line diff.
#
# What is genuinely worth enforcing survives untouched: a key missing from a
# shipped locale still fails CI (l10n_untranslated.json, above), and
# arb_guard_test.dart holds the .arb files themselves to rules the generator
# has no opinion about.
lib/l10n/generated/
